@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "FAQ";
}

<h1><i class="fas fa-circle-question me-2"></i>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>

<hr/>

<div class="row g-4">
    <div class="col-12">
        <div class="card">
            <h5 class="card-header"><i class="fas fa-lock me-2"></i>Q: What does the privacy option on the game mean?</h5>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p>When you create a game you are given the option if the game should be 'publicly' listed. This means that:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>The game may be listed on the homepage as a featured game</li>
                    <li>The game may be listed on other areas of the website</li>
                    <li>The usernames of the game participants (<strong>not emails</strong>) will be visible unless overridden in the user's profile</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-12">
        <div class="card">
            <h5 class="card-header"><i class="fas fa-chess-board me-2"></i>Q: What are the different 'Scrabble' boards?</h5>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p>When you are creating a game you are provided some different options for the board. You can read a detailed breakdown of the differences <a asp-area="" asp-controller="About" asp-action="ScrabbleGames">here</a>.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-12">
        <div class="card">
            <h5 class="card-header"><i class="fas fa-heart me-2"></i>Q: Is this website free?</h5>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p>
                    Yes! This is a personal project and is provided completely free of charge with no limitations on accounts.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@section Styles {

    <link href="~/css/faq.css" rel="stylesheet"/>
}